            <ArticleTitle>Spasm of a saphenous vein bypass graft. A possible mechanism for occlusion of the venous graft.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>413-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The phenomenon of spasm in a venous graft was documented by angiographic study of the graft. This phenomenon has not been reported previously, and, therefore, its frequency of occurrence is unknown. Spasm of a venous graft may prove to play a significant role in the early development of myocardial infarction, closure of the graft, or recurrence of angina after initially successful surgery for aortocoronary bypass when venous grafts remain patent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
